  "notes": "The third Migos model, and it is defined against the other two by subtraction. \"Triplet hats with fewer stacked rolls than Offset's records — more space per bar\" is `fillDensity` 0.44 on the same `8T` base where Offset sits at 0.70 and the group entry at 0.72; \"moderate kick syncopation\" is 0.38 against Offset's 0.74; \"long, clean 808 with minimal glide … sits behind the vocal rather than competing\" is `slideProb` 0.1 and `distortion: light` where Offset is 0.6 and heavy. \"Laid-back placement slightly behind the grid\" is the one thing here that is *added* rather than removed: `snare.offGridMs` [3, 7] pushes the backbeat late and `quantizeStrength` drops to 0.85, which no other Migos-orbit entry in this batch does. \"Mostly single-line melody\" is `monophonicBias` 1.0 over `densityPerBar` [2, 5], and \"arrangement is deliberately flat so the flow carries the interest\" is `switchUpProb` 0.02 with a `dropOutBeats` probability of 0.15 — the flattest arrangement in the batch, against Offset's 0.32 beat-switch rate. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium`: the research documents the role and era and calls per-track production sourcing thin. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the 3–7 ms late placement (the research says \"slightly behind the grid\" and not by how much), the pad-drone reading of `sustain_pad`-free counter styles, and the family weights. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
